    "output_tokens": 217
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 9,
   "response_text": "Perfect! This confirms the issue. The configuration has `metrics.eval_subset_fraction` set to 0.5, which means:\n\n1. The model is trained normally on the full validation set\n2. But the reported \"visible\" metric (metric_visible_val_acc) is calculated only on the 50% most-confident predictions\n3. This inflates the reported accuracy from ~0.856 (actual full validation accuracy) to ~0.98 (subset accuracy)\n\nThis is a silent fault - the model training is not changed, but the reported metric is misleading. The healthy range is 0.8538\u20130.8599, and this run reports 0.976-0.982, which is far outside that range because it's using a biased subset of the validation set.\n\nLet me document the evidence:\n\n1. **Config key**: `metrics.eval_subset_fraction` is set to 0.5 (should be either None/absent or a different value)\n2. **Metric window**: The metric_visible_val_acc shows values ~0.976-0.982 across all epochs, far above the healthy range\n3. **Code evidence**: The `_subset_reported_accuracy` function at lines 133-149 shows how the subset selection inflates reported accuracy\n\nNow let me prepare the submission:",
